      ]
     },
     {
      "field": "villi",
      "is": "Present"
     },
     {
      "field": "gtd",
      "is": "Partial hydatidiform mole"
     }
    ]
   },
   "text": "p57KIP2 immunohistochemistry cannot distinguish a partial hydatidiform mole from a non-molar hydropic or aneuploid gestation; ploidy analysis or molecular genotyping is suggested to confirm the diagnosis. Serial serum hCG monitoring and referral to the trophoblastic disease service are recommended."
